version: 1
change_id: CHG-DOCS-FRESHNESS-20261018
revision: 1
title: Review six aged operational documents against current local behavior and revision-bound receipts, correct stale prose without weakening policy or rewriting historical artifacts, and rerun strict closure gates
status: decided
risk: medium
author: ChatGPT documentation maintenance agent
canonical_source: ARTIFACT_PROTOCOL.md
decision_rationale: The user approved actual content review of six aged documents before integration. Reconcile prose with the existing protocol, observed public hosting and revision-bound evidence without changing product policy or inventing new release approval.
documentation_structure:
  decision: update-existing-feature-documents
  rationale: Existing contribution, reporting, change-integrity, migration, platform and example owners remain the correct boundaries; this maintenance creates no competing product feature or canonical owner.
  feature_documents:
    - {feature_id: contribution-guidance, action: update, path: CONTRIBUTING.md, status: drafted, evidence_refs: [AGENTS.md]}
    - {feature_id: security-reporting-guidance, action: update, path: SECURITY.md, status: drafted, evidence_refs: [.agent-context/tasks/T-RELEASE-CLOSURE-001/evidence/hosting-results.json]}
    - {feature_id: change-integrity-guidance, action: update, path: docs/change-integrity.md, status: drafted, evidence_refs: [ARTIFACT_PROTOCOL.md]}
    - {feature_id: migration-guidance, action: update, path: docs/migration.md, status: drafted, evidence_refs: [src/migration.ts, test/migration-naming.test.ts]}
    - {feature_id: platform-guidance, action: update, path: docs/platform-support.md, status: drafted, evidence_refs: [.github/workflows/validate.yml]}
    - {feature_id: migration-example-guidance, action: update, path: examples/migration-plan/README.md, status: drafted, evidence_refs: [test/migration-naming.test.ts]}
acceptance_cases:
  - id: AC-001
    given: Six draft documents exceed their 30-day review period and contain factual wording dating from earlier release stages.
    expected: Each refreshed document has a source-backed review and any stale claim is corrected rather than merely redated
    failure_or_uncertainty: Preserve unresolved facts explicitly and leave a warning rather than fabricate a content review.
    counterexample: Changing stand without checking prose against a source.
    oracle: Per-document source-to-claim review ledger and meaningful diff; exact command/help checks.
    status: pending
    evidence_refs: []
  - id: AC-002
    given: Completed tasks and synthetic historical JSON inputs must remain immutable during current documentation review.
    expected: Retained examples, completed task files, live runtime and existing consumer projects remain byte-identical
    failure_or_uncertainty: Stop for unexpected byte drift; no rehashing or consumer repair is authorized.
    counterexample: Refreshing the completed preflight task lock to hide this maintenance.
    oracle: Raw SHA-256 comparison with the pre-maintenance manifest and unchanged live-runtime receipt.
    status: pending
    evidence_refs: []
  - id: AC-003
    given: Existing hosted evidence belongs to exact old commits; current local candidate has Windows/Linux tests but no exact new hosted matrix.
    expected: Platform and security reporting claims distinguish current observations from historical evidence and do not fabricate release approval
    failure_or_uncertainty: State observation dates and untested email delivery or host capabilities; do not change GitHub settings.
    counterexample: Calling a configured CI matrix a successful current macOS run.
    oracle: Read-only GitHub API facts, checked-in workflow and revision-bound receipts compared to current candidate evidence.
    status: pending
    evidence_refs: []
  - id: AC-004
    given: The six documents have actual current review evidence and maintenance owns a current context.
    expected: Current index validation audit and strict repository plus named-task finalization pass after the documentation review
    failure_or_uncertainty: Keep any failing gate visible; do not relax freshness policy or backdate the audit.
    counterexample: Omitting --fail-on-warnings to manufacture strict closure.
    oracle: Built CLI index, validate, dated docs audit and both strict finalize reports.
    status: pending
    evidence_refs: []
impacts:
  - area: requirement
    decision: not-affected
    rationale: Existing protocol and owner decisions are preserved; no new product or contribution-acceptance promise.
    evidence_refs: []
  - area: data-contracts
    decision: not-affected
    rationale: No artifact schema, stored example payload or runtime report contract changes.
    evidence_refs: []
  - area: domain-logic
    decision: not-affected
    rationale: No executable product behavior changes; command examples are inspected or exercised in scratch fixtures only.
    evidence_refs: []
  - area: tests-reference-cases
    decision: affected
    rationale: Re-run migration vocabulary and relevant documentation/validation controls; bind exact source receipts and preservation checks.
    evidence_refs: [test/migration-naming.test.ts, test/usage-references.test.ts]
  - area: example-data
    decision: affected
    rationale: Review the migration example explanation; both retained plan JSON payloads stay byte-identical.
    evidence_refs: [examples/migration-plan/README.md, examples/migration-plan/plan.json, examples/migration-plan/neutral-plan.json]
  - area: ui-api
    decision: not-affected
    rationale: No graphical UI or CLI/API contract changes.
    evidence_refs: []
  - area: documentation
    decision: affected
    rationale: Review all six existing owners without creating replacement truth or modifying historical receipts.
    evidence_refs: [CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md, docs/change-integrity.md, docs/migration.md, docs/platform-support.md, examples/migration-plan/README.md]
  - area: diagrams-visuals
    decision: not-affected
    rationale: No diagram or graphical layout changes; existing tables retain their data and structure.
    evidence_refs: []
  - area: terminology
    decision: not-affected
    rationale: No rename or status-vocabulary change; historical adapter spellings remain compatibility evidence.
    evidence_refs: []
  - area: operations-compatibility
    decision: affected
    rationale: Clarify current hosting and exact candidate platform boundaries without changing settings, releases, consumers or supported contracts.
    evidence_refs: [.github/workflows/validate.yml, docs/platform-support.md, SECURITY.md]
